{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Thus.</b> I have sent to Babylon. Some say that the vav of שלחתי alludes to the prophet, but in my opinion it is the word of YHWH, for at first it says 'Thus said YHWH,' and afterward 'I am YHWH, your Holy One.' And the meaning is: I have come so swiftly, as though I have sent. And a great sage in Spain said that the Glory speaks with the prophet, and he is the prince of Israel, the one sent to Babylon to redeem Israel." "<b>And I will bring down bars.</b> The bars of Babylon, and it was trapped, like the meaning of 'her bars are lost and broken' (Lamentations 2:9) — the gates of the city." "<b>And Chaldeans, etc.</b> And I will bring down Chaldeans who are in ships — their song — I will bring them down from the ships."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 43, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:57:46.261602860Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}